From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:29:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Embedding: x87 stack faults raise invalid operation

x87 marks each register empty or full, and an embedding host that runs
x86 programs exactly needs what those tags decide. With the precise
stack an embedding host uses, a read of an empty register is now a
stack underflow and a push onto a full one a stack overflow: either
raises invalid operation and the stack fault flag, sets C1 for an
overflow and clears it for an underflow, sets ES and B while the
control word unmasks invalid operation, and goes on with the QNaN
indefinite. Every pop leaves its register empty. FXAM reads its
operand without a stack fault, because it classifies an empty
register.
---
 .../Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher/X87.cpp   |  24 ++++-
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json           |   5 +-
 .../IR/Passes/x87StackOptimizationPass.cpp    | 101 ++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 117 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

